{
  "id": "compost-stages",
  "title": "The composting cycle",
  "claim": "A pile passes through five stages, each with its own expected readings, over about seven weeks. Peak decomposition is the stretch held at 55 °C or above, where pathogens die. The simulator and the emulator generate their readings from these ranges, and the stage model learned from them.",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "s0",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 1,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Early mesophilic",
      "tag": "stage 0",
      "tone": "amber",
      "fields": [
        "temperature // 28–45 °C",
        "moisture // 60–65 %",
        "O₂ // 15.5–21 %",
        "CO₂ // 0.5–5.5 %",
        "days // about 2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 2,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Active thermophilic",
      "tag": "stage 1",
      "tone": "amber",
      "fields": [
        "temperature // 45–60 °C",
        "moisture // 55–60 %",
        "O₂ // 12–17.5 %",
        "CO₂ // 3.5–9 %",
        "days // about 3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 3,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Peak decomposition",
      "tag": "stage 2",
      "tone": "amber",
      "accent": true,
      "fields": [
        "*temperature // 55–65 °C",
        "moisture // 50–58 %",
        "O₂ // 10–16.5 %",
        "CO₂ // 4.5–11 %",
        "days // about 5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 4,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Cooling",
      "tag": "stage 3",
      "tone": "amber",
      "fields": [
        "temperature // 60 down to 30 °C",
        "moisture // 45–55 %",
        "O₂ // 11–20 %",
        "CO₂ // 1–10 %",
        "days // about 8"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 5,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Maturation",
      "tag": "stage 4",
      "tone": "green",
      "fields": [
        "temperature // 28–32 °C",
        "moisture // 40–50 %",
        "O₂ // 19–21 %",
        "CO₂ // 0.3–2 %",
        "days // about 30"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "from": "s0",
      "to": "s1",
      "label": "heats up"
    },
    {
      "from": "s1",
      "to": "s2",
      "label": "peaks"
    },
    {
      "from": "s2",
      "to": "s3",
      "label": "cools"
    },
    {
      "from": "s3",
      "to": "s4",
      "label": "settles"
    }
  ],
  "legend": {
    "call": "the pile moves on",
    "accent": "pathogen-kill target"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Holding 55 °C or more for three days in a row kills pathogens: the EPA Class A sanitation target. Peak decomposition starts once the core has held 55 °C for 6 hours. A bin that never gets that hot, like a small Takakura basket, goes straight from active thermophilic to cooling.",
    "The ranges, their sources and the ammonia level (0 to 1, relative, not ppm) are in `simulator/composting_stages.py`. The floor is 28 °C because the pilot site in Mataram is 24 to 32 °C outside.",
    "The API estimates a real bin's stage with a model trained in `ml/` on cycles simulated from these ranges. Alerts use their own fixed limits."
  ]
}